text: "# Examples — social SEO in practice\n\nWorked optimizations showing keyword research → placement across the surface → cluster thinking, plus\nhonest scope. Subject: a solo founder building a SaaS social scheduler. Voice context is the blunt\nindie-founder voice; your output uses the loaded `voice.md`, `audience.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Example 1 — optimizing one TikTok for search\n\n**Target query (from autocomplete):** \"how to schedule social media posts for free\" (typed the seed,\nTikTok suggested it — real demand, no invented volume).\n**Optimization (triple mention):**\n- **Spoken (first 3s):** \"Here's how to schedule social media posts for free…\"\n- **On-screen text:** `Schedule posts for free` (keyword headline, not decoration).\n- **Caption:** \"How to schedule your social media posts for free — the exact setup I use. [natural\n  context]\" + 3 niche hashtags.\n- **Cluster note:** this is one of a set — pair with \"schedule Instagram posts,\" \"best free scheduler,\"\n  \"schedule a week of content in 20 min\" → becomes the answer for *scheduling* on the FYP and in search.\n\n## Example 2 — Instagram (name field + caption + alt)\n\n**Move people miss:** the **name field**. Change \"Maya R.\" → **\"Maya · Social Scheduling Tips\"** so the\naccount surfaces when people search the category, not just the handle.\n**Post:** caption leads with the natural keyword (\"how to batch a week of content…\"), Reel is captioned,\nalt text describes the carousel in searchable terms. 5 niche hashtags max.\n\n## Example 3 — YouTube Short\n\n- **Title:** \"How to Schedule a Week of Social Posts in 20 Minutes (Free)\" — keyword-led, descriptive.\n- **Description:** ~200 words of natural context + the steps + a link; not one line.\n- **Captions** uploaded; **chapters** if long-form (\"00:20 The free tool,\" \"01:10 Batch the captions\").\n- Same phrase in the spoken intro. Works for the Short *and* Google's video panel.\n\n## Example 4 — Pinterest pin\n\nKeywords are everything (no hashtags). **Pin title:** \"Free Social Media Scheduling Setup.\"\n**Description:** keyword-rich, intent-matching (\"plan and auto-publish a week of posts for free…\").\n**Board:** \"Social Media Scheduling\" (a topic cluster). Alt + on-image text describe it. Evergreen —\nkeeps surfacing for planners for months.\n\n## Example 5 — a keyword cluster (the real strategy)\n\nPillar: **\"saving time on social.\"** Cluster of evergreen posts, each on one long-tail query:\nbatch-scheduling, free tools, repurposing one idea across platforms, a realistic weekly cadence,\ncaptions fast. Across TikTok/IG/YouTube/Pinterest. Result: the account becomes *the* searchable answer\nfor time-strapped founders — and the recommendation algorithm categorizes it cleanly too.\n\n---\n\n## Honest scope (say this)\n\n- **Searchability, not a #1 guarantee** — you optimize the signals; the algorithm + competition decide\n  the rank.\n- **No invented volumes** — research is autocomplete / related / native analytics / tools, not numbers\n  the agent made up.\n- **No keyword stuffing** — natural language, primary keyword once or twice; spam dilutes your signal.\n- **Evergreen compounds** — the payoff builds over months; it's not a one-post trick.\n- **GEO is separate** — getting cited by ChatGPT/Google AI is `ai-search-optimization`'s job.\n- **No WoopSocial analytics** — WoopSocial publishes the optimized content; the search read-out comes\n  from native platform insights (+ Search Console/UTMs).\n\n---\n\n## What the examples share\n\n- They start from a **real query** (autocomplete), not a guess.\n- They place the keyword across the platform's **specific indexed surfaces** (triple mention where it\n  applies).\n- They think in **clusters / evergreen**, not one-off posts.\n- They lead with **keywords, support with hashtags**, in **natural language**.\n"
